    <Placemark>
      <name>Athens (Acropolis) (אתונה (יוון))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Athens (Acropolis) (אתונה (יוון))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Greece</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.3.a (Pages 99)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A cave leading to an underground corridor with a spring at its base, accessed by eight flights of stairs from the Acropolis. The entrance was sealed during sieges. Pottery dates the end of its use to the second half of the 13th century BCE.</p>]]></description>
