    <Placemark>
      <name>Mezer (מצר)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Mezer (מצר)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Tunnel Shaft</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Sinai / Egypt</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.4 (Pages 100, 101)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A deep water shaft, 52m deep, with a staircase descending along its side, dug to reach groundwater. The excavation was documented in two texts and took 100 days with 120 workers. The bottom was moist, suggesting groundwater was reached.</p>]]></description>
