    <Placemark>
      <name>Mycenae (מיקנה (יוון))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Mycenae (מיקנה (יוון))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Ancient City Water System</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Greece</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.3.b (Pages 99, 100)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>An underground system with hidden clay pipes transporting water from the Perseia spring (360m away) to an internal reservoir within the city walls, accessed by a stepped passage. Dated to the 13th century BCE. Additionally, two wells were found within the city walls, and two external springs served settlements outside the walls.</p>]]></description>
