    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Ashdod (תל אשדוד)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Ashdod (תל אשדוד)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.8 (Pages 103, 104)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A plastered pool (4162) measuring 3.2x1.5m, found in Area G within a governor&apos;s house or palace (Strata XIV-XVII, Late Bronze Age II). It had two phases, with a brick layer beneath the plaster floor, and a drainage channel leading to a stone-lined drainage pit. Water likely collected from roofs or was manually brought from a well.</p>]]></description>
