    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Gamma (תל ג&apos;מה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Gamma (תל ג&apos;מה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.2 (Pages 98)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A sealed well, evidenced by large stones with rope marks and a depression that fills with water, located 400m southwest of Nahal Besor, at the foot of the acropolis. Possibly dates to the initial phase of the lower city in the Late Bronze Age.</p>]]></description>
