    <Placemark>
      <name>Tiryns (טירינס (יוון))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tiryns (טירינס (יוון))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Greece</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.3.c (Pages 100)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Two steep underground passages (30m long, 10m within walls) led through the 10m thick walls to two subterranean cisterns fed by springs. The passages, covered by corbelled arches, ended in small basins where water seeped from rock fissures.</p>]]></description>
